This is not an open-source licence. The source code is published so that you can
read it, run it and adapt it to your own forum. Please read the terms below before
you use the software.


1. Definitions

"Software" means the Divan forum software in this repository, in source form.
"Vendor" means Web Danışmanı, the owner of the Software.
"Licence code" means the code the Vendor issues for one installation of the
Software through https://webdanismani.com.
"Installation" means one running copy of the Software, serving one forum at one
address.


2. What you may do

Provided that you keep to this licence, the Vendor allows you, free of charge:

a) to install and run the Software, for personal or commercial purposes, on
   Installations that each hold a valid Licence code of their own;
b) to run additional copies for development and testing that are not open to the
   public;
c) to read the source code and to change it for use on your own Installations;
d) to send your changes back to the Vendor (for example as a pull request).


3. Licence code

Every Installation needs its own Licence code. The code for the Software itself is
free of charge and is issued through the Vendor's shop at https://webdanismani.com.
A code is tied to the address of the Installation it is activated on; it can be
released from that Installation and used at another address.

The Vendor may suspend or cancel a Licence code that is used against this licence.


4. What you may not do

You may not:

a) distribute, publish, sell, rent, lend or sublicense the Software or any modified
   version of it, in whole or in part, to anyone else. Publishing your own fork
   on a code hosting service is allowed only where the service's terms give other
   users no more than the right to view it and to prepare changes for the Vendor's
